            <h2 id="scope">1. Scope & definitions</h2>
            <p class="muted">This Policy governs processing of personal data by JOOD in connection with our websites, mobile applications, marketing activities, order fulfilment, customer support, and other services. <strong>Personal data</strong> means any information that identifies or can reasonably be used to identify a living person.</p>

            <h2 id="data-we-collect">2. Data we collect</h2>
            <p class="muted">We collect data necessary to provide services and operate our business. Categories of data include:</p>
            <ul class="muted value-list">
              <li><strong>Identity & contact:</strong> full name, email, telephone, shipping & billing addresses.</li>
              <li><strong>Account & credentials:</strong> username, password (securely hashed), profile preferences.</li>
              <li><strong>Payment & billing:</strong> payment tokens, transaction references (sensitive card data is handled by PCI-compliant providers and not retained by us).</li>
              <li><strong>Communications:</strong> support tickets, emails, call recordings (where permitted).</li>
              <li><strong>Technical & usage:</strong> IP address, device identifiers, browser type, pages visited, search queries, referrer URLs, and cookies/analytics data.</li>
              <li><strong>Marketing & engagement:</strong> opt-in status, email open/click history, and preferences.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 id="legal-basis">3. Legal basis & purposes for processing</h2>
            <p class="muted">We only process personal data where we have a lawful basis, including:</p>
            <ul class="muted value-list">
              <li><strong>Contractual necessity:</strong> to fulfil orders, provide purchased goods and services, manage returns and warranties.</li>
              <li><strong>Legal compliance:</strong> to comply with tax, accounting, anti-money laundering or other legal obligations.</li>
              <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> for fraud prevention, platform security, analytics and business operations, subject to a balancing test.</li>
              <li><strong>Consent:</strong> where you have given consent (for example, marketing communications and certain cookies). You may withdraw consent at any time.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 id="how-we-use">4. How we use personal data (processing activities)</h2>
            <p class="muted">Examples of processing activities and the purposes they serve:</p>
            <table class="table" aria-describedby="processing-examples">
              <thead>
                <tr><th>Processing</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Order processing</td><td>Validate, fulfil and deliver purchases, manage refunds and returns.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Customer support</td><td>Respond to enquiries, resolve disputes, and provide product support.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Payment reconciliation</td><td>Record transactions, prevent fraud, and maintain financial records.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Marketing (with consent)</td><td>Send offers, newsletters and product updates tailored to your preferences.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Analytics & product improvement</td><td>Measure site performance, test features, and improve user experience.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <h2 id="sharing">5. Sharing & third parties</h2>
            <p class="muted">We do not sell your personal data. We may share data with trusted third parties who act for us under contract and are required to protect your data. These include:</p>
            <ul class="muted value-list">
              <li>Payment processors and gateways for transaction authorisation.</li>
              <li>Logistics, warehousing and delivery partners for order fulfilment.</li>
              <li>Customer support platforms for ticketing and live chat services.</li>
              <li>Analytics, monitoring and hosting providers to operate and secure our Services.</li>
              <li>Legal and professional advisors for compliance and dispute resolution.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="muted">We require contractual safeguards (data processing agreements) and, where applicable, technical and organisational measures from our providers.</p>

            <h2 id="transfers">6. International transfers</h2>
            <p class="muted">Personal data may be processed or hosted in jurisdictions outside the UAE. When we transfer data internationally, we ensure appropriate safeguards are in place such as standard contractual clauses, data processing agreements, and other lawful mechanisms to protect your information.</p>

            <h2 id="cookies">7. Cookies & tracking technologies</h2>
            <p class="muted">We use cookies, pixels and similar technologies to provide core functionality, remember preferences and measure performance. You can manage cookie preferences via our cookie banner or through your browser settings. Below is a summary of cookie categories:</p>
            <table class="table">
              <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Retention</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Essential</td><td>Required for shopping cart, login and secure sessions</td><td>Session</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Performance</td><td>Collect anonymous usage to improve site speed and reliability</td><td>1 year</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Functional</td><td>Remember preferences and language selection</td><td>1 year</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Advertising</td><td>Deliver interest-based ads and measure campaigns</td><td>varies (up to 24 months)</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <h2 id="retention">8. Data retention</h2>
            <p class="muted">We retain personal data only as long as necessary for the purposes described and to meet legal obligations. Typical retention periods:</p>
            <ul class="muted value-list">
              <li>Order & transaction records: <strong>7 years</strong> (to meet tax, accounting and audit requirements).</li>
              <li>Customer support records: <strong>2–5 years</strong> depending on complexity and legal needs.</li>
              <li>Marketing preferences: until you opt out or request deletion.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="muted">When data is no longer required we delete or irreversibly anonymise it.</p>

            <h2 id="security">9. Security controls</h2>
            <p class="muted">We adopt a defence-in-depth approach combining organisational, technical and physical controls. Key measures include:</p>
            <ul class="muted value-list">
              <li>Transport-level encryption (TLS) for data in transit.</li>
              <li>Encryption at rest for sensitive datasets where applicable.</li>
              <li>Role-based access control and periodic access reviews.</li>
              <li>Secure development lifecycle, dependency scanning, and patch management.</li>
              <li>Regular security testing, audits and third-party penetration tests.</li>
              <li>Incident response plan and forensic procedures to investigate events.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="muted">Although we apply industry best practices, no system is 100% secure; we continually improve our safeguards.</p>

            <h2 id="rights">10. Your rights & how to exercise them</h2>
            <p class="muted">Subject to applicable law you may have rights including:</p>
            <ul class="muted value-list">
              <li>Right to access: request a copy of the personal data we hold.</li>
              <li>Right to correction: ask us to correct inaccurate information.</li>
              <li>Right to erasure: request deletion where there is no lawful reason to retain data.</li>
              <li>Right to object or restrict processing: where processing is based on legitimate interests or direct marketing.</li>
              <li>Right to portability: request transfer of your data to another controller where feasible.</li>
              <li>Right to withdraw consent: where processing is based on consent.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="muted">To exercise any right, contact our Data Protection Officer (DPO) at <a href="mailto:dpo@jood.com">dpo@jood.com</a>. We will verify your identity and respond within applicable legal timeframes (typically within 30 days). If we cannot comply, we will explain the reason and applicable remedies.</p>

            <h2 id="automated">11. Automated decision-making & profiling</h2>
            <p class="muted">We may use automated systems to personalise offers, product recommendations, and email content. These systems do not generally make decisions that produce legal effects. If automated decisions with significant effects are used, we will provide information about the logic, data and your rights to request human review.</p>

            <h2 id="children">12. Children's privacy</h2>
            <p class="muted">Our Services are not directed to children under 16 years. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children. If you believe we have inadvertently collected a child's data, contact us and we will promptly remove it.</p>

            <h2 id="breach">13. Data breach & notification</h2>
            <p class="muted">We maintain an incident response program. In the event of a personal data breach likely to result in a high risk to individuals’ rights and freedoms, we will:</p>
            <ul class="muted value-list">
              <li>Notify affected individuals without undue delay, including the nature of the breach and recommended steps.</li>
              <li>Notify relevant supervisory authorities in accordance with legal requirements.</li>
              <li>Provide remedial measures and support to affected individuals (where appropriate).</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="muted">We document all incidents and post-incident remediation actions to prevent recurrence.</p>

            <h2 id="contact">14. Contact & complaints</h2>
            <p class="muted">For privacy enquiries or to exercise your rights, please contact:</p>
            <p class="muted"><strong>Data Protection Officer (DPO)</strong><br>
              Email: <a href="mailto:dpo@jood.com">dpo@jood.com</a><br>
              Phone: +971-55-555-5555<br>
              Address: Al Reem Tower, Dubai, UAE</p>
            <p class="muted">If you remain unsatisfied after contacting us, you may lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority or the relevant UAE regulator. We will cooperate with supervisory authorities and follow applicable dispute-resolution procedures.</p>

            <h2 id="changes">15. Changes to this policy</h2>
            <p class="muted">We may amend this Policy to reflect regulatory, operational or business changes. Material changes will be communicated via the website (notice on this page and/or email to registered users). Please check the effective date at the top of this page. </p>
          </article>
        </div>

